# Examples too slow for a hosted CI job: run them by hand. Every one is a MEASUREMENT, not a gate.
#
# A hosted runner stops a job at six hours, and these take longer than that on one core, so neither
# the per-push step nor the weekly one can run them in full. Dropping them from CI entirely would
# bring back the defect running examples on CI was introduced to catch -- an example nobody runs
# stops running, and nobody notices (`dtm_scale` panicked on a missing argument for as long as that
# was true). So the weekly job runs each of these with FERROTHERM_EXAMPLE_SMOKE=1, which every
# example listed here must honour: the same code at sizes that finish in minutes, with a banner
# saying its numbers are not the measurement. The full run, and the numbers worth quoting, are by hand.
#
# EMPTY SINCE 2026-09-28. The two examples that were here, penalty_mixing and informed_scaling_exact,
# each spent their three hours summing a lag series one application of the kernel at a time. Both now
# solve the fundamental-matrix system matrix-free (autocorr::tau_int_solved) and finish in under seven
# minutes of CPU, so they run in full in the weekly job (examples/SLOW) and their smoke modes are gone.
# An empty list is a state the weekly job accepts; a listed example still needs a smoke mode.
#
